Install the page clock before you navigate, so the counter's script starts on the controlled clock:

```js
async page => {
  await page.clock.install({ time: 0 });
  await page.goto('http://127.0.0.1:4173/');
  const now = await page.evaluate(() => Date.now());
  await page.clock.pauseAt(now + 1000);
  // step with runFor and sample each frame
}
```

Before `goto`, register an init script that pauses each CSS animation as it starts:

```js
await page.addInitScript(() => {
  addEventListener('animationstart', e => { for (const a of e.target.getAnimations()) a.pause(); }, true);
});
```
The hero's entrance is then still at its first frames when the page has loaded.

